{
  "definition": "Y is a direct caller of X if running Y's own body can call X with no other repo-defined named function in between. Lambdas, comprehensions and generator expressions belong to the function they appear in. Module-level code belongs to the module. Decorator wrappers are real functions. Truth is what the program does at runtime, not what a static tool can see. Only repo-defined symbols count. impact expects the full set of transitive callers within the given depth, tests included. A constructor call targets Class.__init__ when the class defines one in source, else the class itself (for example a dataclass).",
  "queries": [
    {"id": "S1", "fixture": "shop", "kind": "callers", "symbol": "shop.models.Order.add_item", "group": "typed receivers",
     "note": "receiver is a local assigned from a constructor call",
     "expected": ["shop.service.OrderService.place_order", "tests.test_pricing.test_percent_discount_and_tax"]},
    {"id": "S2", "fixture": "shop", "kind": "callers", "symbol": "shop.pricing.price_order", "group": "imports",
     "note": "called through `import ... as quote` and a plain from-import",
